# This is the key file for your AI operating system.
#
# What it is for: every password, API key, token and app password your
# assistant needs to reach a tool lives in .env, and nowhere else. Never in a
# markdown file, never in a chat, never in a commit. Git ignores .env, so it
# can never be pushed to GitHub or saved into the history.
#
# How it works: the setup script copies this file to .env. When a tool is
# connected, the assistant writes the KEY NAME here and the owner pastes the
# value in themselves. The connection file in System/Connections/ names the
# key, never the value.
#
# Rules:
# - One key per line, KEY_NAME=value, no spaces around the equals sign.
# - Lines starting with # are notes. Empty values are fine until a tool is connected.
# - Claude is blocked from reading .env by .claude/settings.json. If it needs a
#   value it asks you to paste it into the tool, never into the chat.
# - Back this file up somewhere private. It is the one file git does not keep.
#
# Examples of the kind of key that goes here, filled in only when that tool is
# connected. Leave the ones you do not use empty or delete the line.

# Email, if the assistant sends or reads mail through a script in Tools/
# GMAIL_APP_PASSWORD=

# A messaging bot, if one is set up later
# TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=

# Any other tool the assistant reaches through a script
# EXAMPLE_API_KEY=
